= BITwiki Visual Diagram Specification: Standards for Knowledge Visualization =

== Purpose ==

This document specifies standards for visual diagrams in BITwiki. Visual diagrams complement textual knowledge, enabling rapid comprehension of complex relationships and structures.

== Diagram Types ==

=== 1. Concept Maps ===

'''Purpose:''' Show relationships between concepts.

'''Elements:'''
* Nodes: Concepts (boxes)
* Edges: Relationships (lines with labels)
* Direction: Optional arrows

'''Example:'''
```
[Feedback] --causes--> [Stability]
   |
   --enables--
   v
[Adaptation]
```

'''Use Cases:'''
* Ontology visualization
* Knowledge relationships
* Causal chains

'''Standards:'''
* Nodes: Rounded rectangles
* Edges: Labeled arrows
* Layout: Hierarchical or force-directed
* Colors: Semantic (blue=idea, green=implementation)

=== 2. Flowcharts ===

'''Purpose:''' Show processes and decision paths.

'''Elements:'''
* Start/End: Ovals
* Process: Rectangles
* Decision: Diamonds
* Arrows: Flow direction

'''Example:'''
```
[Start] --> [Validate Claim] --> {Valid?}
                              |Yes
                              v
                        [Add to BITwiki]
                              |
                              v
                           [End]
```

'''Use Cases:'''
* Validation protocols
* Editorial workflows
* Decision trees

'''Standards:'''
* Start/End: Oval
* Process: Rectangle
* Decision: Diamond
* Flow: Top-to-bottom, left-to-right

=== 3. Hierarchical Diagrams ===

'''Purpose:''' Show taxonomic relationships.

'''Elements:'''
* Root: Top node
* Branches: Intermediate nodes
* Leaves: Terminal nodes
* Lines: Parent-child relationships

'''Example:'''
```
Systems Science
├── Cybernetics
│   ├── First-Order
│   └── Second-Order
└── Information Theory
    ├── Entropy
    └── Channel Capacity
```

'''Use Cases:'''
* Taxonomy visualization
* Category hierarchies
* Organizational structures

'''Standards:'''
* Root at top
* Children below parents
* Consistent spacing
* Collapsible branches

=== 4. Network Diagrams ===

'''Purpose:''' Show connections in a system.

'''Elements:'''
* Nodes: Entities (circles)
* Edges: Connections (lines)
* Weights: Optional (line thickness)

'''Example:'''
```
    [A] --- [B]
     |       |
     |       |
    [C] --- [D]
```

'''Use Cases:'''
* Knowledge graphs
* Social networks
* System architectures

'''Standards:'''
* Nodes: Circles or icons
* Edges: Lines (directed or undirected)
* Layout: Force-directed or circular
* Clustering: Group related nodes

=== 5. Temporal Diagrams ===

'''Purpose:''' Show events over time.

'''Elements:'''
* Timeline: Horizontal or vertical axis
* Events: Markers on timeline
* Duration: Bars spanning time
* Milestones: Key points

'''Example:'''
```
1948 ---- 1960 ---- 1972 ---- 1984 ---- 1996 ---- 2008 ---- 2020
  |         |         |         |         |         |         |
Wiener   Ashby   von Foerster  Maturana  Luhmann   BITwiki   Future
```

'''Use Cases:'''
* Historical timelines
* Project schedules
* Evolution of ideas

'''Standards:'''
* Time flows left-to-right
* Events marked clearly
* Scale consistent
* Milestones highlighted

== Notation Standards ==

=== Mermaid.js === ===

BITwiki uses Mermaid.js for diagram generation:

'''Flowchart:'''
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Start] --> B{Is it?}
    B -->|Yes| C[OK]
    C --> D[Rethink]
    D --> B
    B ---->|No| E[End]
```

'''Sequence Diagram:'''
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Contributor
    participant B as Validator
    A->>B: Submit claim
    B->>A: Request evidence
    A->>B: Provide sources
    B->>A: Approve
```

'''Class Diagram:'''
```mermaid
classDiagram
    class Idea {
        +String name
        +Float confidence
        +validate()
    }
    class Implementation {
        +String technology
        +deploy()
    }
    Idea <|-- Implementation
```

=== Graphviz === ===

For complex network diagrams:

```dot
digraph G {
    rankdir=TB;
    node [shape=box, style=rounded];

    A [label="Systems Science"];
    B [label="Cybernetics"];
    C [label="Information Theory"];

    A -> B;
    A -> C;
}
```

=== Color Semantics ===

| Color | Meaning | Example |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Blue (#0066CC) | Ideas, concepts | Feedback loop |
| Green (#009900) | Implementations | Neural network |
| Gray (#666666) | Topics, categories | Cybernetics |
| Orange (#FF6600) | Projects | Research effort |
| Purple (#9900CC) | Protocols | Methods |
| Red (#CC0000) | Deprecated, errors | Superseded theory |
=== Line Styles ===

| Style | Meaning | Example |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Solid | Confirmed relationship | Causes |
| Dashed | Hypothetical relationship | May cause |
| Dotted | Weak relationship | Related to |
| Thick | Strong relationship | Directly causes |
| Thin | Weak relationship | Indirectly related |
=== Node Shapes ===

| Shape | Meaning | Example |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Rectangle | Process, action | Validation step |
| Rounded rectangle | Concept, idea | Feedback |
| Oval | Start/end | Terminal node |
| Diamond | Decision | Branch point |
| Circle | Entity | Person, object |
| Hexagon | Protocol | Method |


== Accessibility ==

=== Text Alternatives ===

Every diagram must have:
* '''Alt text:''' Brief description
* '''Long description:''' Detailed explanation
* '''Data table:''' Tabular equivalent

'''Example:'''
```html
<figure>
    <img src="diagram.png" alt="Concept map showing feedback relationships">
    <figcaption>Figure 1: Feedback relationships in cybernetic systems. 
    [Detailed description: Feedback loop connects sensor, controller, and actuator...]</figcaption>
</figure>
```

=== Color Blindness ===
* Use patterns, not just colors
* Ensure contrast ratios meet WCAG 2.1
* Provide color-independent labels

'''Good:'''
* Blue solid line: Established
* Blue dashed line: Emerging
* Red solid line: Contradicts

'''Bad:'''
* Blue: Established
* Green: Emerging
* Red: Contradicts

=== Screen Readers ===
* Diagrams must be navigable
* Nodes must be labeled
* Relationships must be described

== Implementation ==

=== Supported Formats ===

| Format | Use Case | Notes |
|--------|----------|-------|
| SVG | Static diagrams | Scalable, accessible |
| Mermaid | Text-based diagrams | Version controlled |
| Graphviz | Automatic layout | Complex graphs |
| PNG | Raster fallback | When SVG not supported |

=== Mermaid Example ===

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Feedback Loop] -->|causes| B[Stability]
    A -->|enables| C[Adaptation]
    B -->|results in| D[Homeostasis]
    C -->|leads to| D
```

=== Graphviz Example ===

```dot
digraph cybernetics {
    node [shape=box, style=rounded];
    feedback -> stability [label="causes"];
    feedback -> adaptation [label="enables"];
    stability -> homeostasis [label="results in"];
    adaptation -> homeostasis [label="leads to"];
}
```

